  "id": "withdrawal-reflex",
  "term": "withdrawal reflex",
  "definition": "Withdrawal reflex is an automatic, involuntary pulling back of a body part when a stimulus is felt as painful or uncomfortable. It can be assessed by observing this response to such stimulation.",
